    "body": "﻿fix on issue/1696-report-button Â· PR #1798 Â· pinned by report_tests (7: the_url_prefills_the_blank_template_with_title_body_and_label, url_encode_keeps_safe_words_and_plains_the_rest, the_body_carries_the_questions_and_the_debug_report, the_title_field_travels_into_the_url, copy_screenshot_says_the_word_on_an_empty_document, the_door_opens_the_window_and_a_kind_button_files_the_url, the_screenshot_paints_the_document) plus the shell_structure and tree_rows_badges_and_actions_are_svg_mastered pins Â· merges at the next cut\n\nQuick gate green on head 984b2af6: camcraft-ui lib suite 793 passed, report_tests 7, structural 10, op_icon_table 5, clippy 0 warnings, icons --check 0 breaches.\n\nCorrection: an earlier version of this comment said the maintainer had GUI-tested this build first. That was wrong. He has not tested it yet. His rule: no push of a fix before his GUI test. The branch and the draft PR now exist on the fork, but the PR stays a draft until his test passes and the independent review is clean. The ready flag was set and has been withdrawn.\n\nTest build: .claude/worktrees/issue-1696/target/debug/camcraft-ui.exe\n\nNote: this PR touches .github/, so pr-test.yml refuses it; the review builds locally (read, not built). Label swap claimed -> in-review needs write access (tbrasselle has none); this comment records the state.\r\n",
